  "id": "COMPOUND:39325 - PROTEIN:6323",
  "verbalization": "The compound in question, (3S,5R,10S,13S,14S,17S)-17-[(E,2R)-6-hydroxy-6-methylhept-4-en-2-yl]-4,4,10,13,14-pentamethyl-2,3,5,6,7,11,12,15,16,17-decahydro-1H-cyclopenta[a]phenanthren-3-ol, is a potential inhibitor of DNA polymerase iota. This is supported by multiple evidence paths, all of which indicate that the compound interacts with DNA polymerase iota through a series of molecular targets. ME-180, a known target of the compound, is itself a target of Lycernuic acid A and Neopyrrolomycin D, both of which are implicated in inhibiting DNA polymerase iota. The evidence suggests that the compound may act as a competitive inhibitor of DNA polymerase iota, potentially by interfering with its enzymatic activity. The strength of the evidence is consistent across the paths, with scores ranging from 0.4686 to 0.5036, indicating a moderate level of confidence in the relationship. The mechanism of action is not fully elucidated, but the presence of multiple targets in the pathway suggests a complex regulatory network involving DNA polymerase iota. The evidence supports the hypothesis that the compound may play a role in modulating DNA polymerase iota activity, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm this relationship.",
